## 3. Truths to carry forward (so nobody re-derives them)

- GPU is not the bottleneck at 1–2 sessions; CPU is 7 % busy; the render path is
  exonerated. Per-frame work only matters for **density** (cost), and density is
  bounded by GPU time, which Rust does not change.
- Production blend is 0.79 ms. "15.9 ms cv2 morphology" is a CLI-prep number.
  GPU blending has no runtime value.
- VAE decode (~8 ms, does not batch) is half the GPU time per frame and the
  biggest single per-frame lever; UNet halves again going batch 4 → 8.
- All TASK-* numbers are from the fork stack (torch 2.11/cu128); production is
  torch 2.1.0/cu121. Re-measure on production before quoting.
- Multi-session is structurally present (`WebRTCServer.sessions`, one render
  service) and **unvalidated**; all sessions serialise on one render thread.
- The talk ratio (~35 %) and "GPU 15 % busy with idle skip" are assumptions.
  `/metrics` can measure them in a week (Q7).
- `cudnn.benchmark = False` and TASK-020 are one-flag experiments that were
  written down and never run.

