## 6. 30 fps — aspirational, last

**Owner's call (2026-09-16):** the last experiment, after everything else has
settled. It is not scheduled and appears in no table above. Kept here so the
unknowns are on record when the time comes.

| Aspect | What changes | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Budget | 40 ms → 33 ms per frame; render is 16.6 ms, VP8 ~7.7 ms on its own thread | fits for 1 session; density −20 % |
| Audio → prompt mapping | whisper features are 50 Hz, mapped 2-per-frame at 25 fps. At 30 fps the mapping is fractional; `StreamingMuseTalkFeatureExtractor(fps=...)` takes `fps`, but whether the windowing is time-based or frame-count-based must be checked before trusting it | **unknown — check first** |
| Source cycle | if the avatar video is 25 fps, replaying its 1874-frame cycle at 30 fps makes head motion 20 % faster, or needs interpolation | likely the most visible effect |
| Bandwidth | +20 % frames at the same bitrate ⇒ fewer bits per frame; raise bitrate or accept softer frames | interacts with Q8 |
| Idle cache | unchanged (cycle index, not time) | — |
| Measurement | `quality_gate` cannot compare 25 vs 30 fps frame-for-frame; compare per-time (nearest frame) plus a human A/B | needs a small script change |

Recommendation: a flag, the extractor check, then a human A/B of the same 30 s
turn at 25 and 30 fps. If the source video is 25 fps, expect the honest answer
to be "smoother mouth, oddly fast head", and stop there unless a 30 fps source
is recorded.

